<title>FRANCE: Canal Plus sees three bln ffr profit on.</title>
<headline>Canal Plus sees three bln ffr profit on.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pay television group Canal Plus said on Friday it expected to make a profit of some three billion francs on two transactions with the Kirch Group signed on Friday.</p>
<p>Canal Plus will sell its 37.5 percent stake in German pay television group Premiere to Kirch. This transaction will be submitted to other Premiere owner Bertelsmann and the German anti-trust and media authorities.</p>
<p>Canal Plus will buy Kirch's 45 percent stake in Telepiu of Italy. The French company said both companies were valued at $1,250 per subscriber.</p>
</text>
